<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Direct download: HARDENED RUNTIME, no App Sandbox.

  Notarisation requires the hardened runtime. The sandbox is deliberately not
  applied here: a direct build is not distributed by Apple, and sandboxing it
  would add a container without adding any guarantee the user is relying on.

  The two allowances below are what a bundled CPython actually needs. Neither
  is decorative and neither should be copied into the App Store entitlements,
  where they invite rejection:

    * allow-unsigned-executable-memory — CPython and several of its extension
      modules allocate writable-executable pages. Without this the app is
      killed at launch by the runtime, with a crash log that names no cause.

    * disable-library-validation — PyInstaller collects dylibs from wheels
      that carry their own signatures from other teams. Library validation
      refuses to load a library signed by a different Team ID, so the app dies
      importing Qt.

  Nothing else is requested. No camera, no microphone, no location, no address
  book, no Apple Events: the app uses none of them, and an entitlement it does
  not use is something to justify later for no benefit now.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
